hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15924","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Abu Burda ibn Niyar: that he slaughtered before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered, so he commanded him to repeat. He said: I find nothing but a jadha'a. So he commanded him to slaughter it."
"15925","Waki' narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abd Allah ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from al-Jahm ibn Abi al-Jahm, from Ibn Niyar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The world shall not pass away until it belongs to Luka' son of Luka'."
"15926","Hashim and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said, Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, he said, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Burda: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No flogging above ten lashes except in a hadd from the hudud of Allah the Exalted."
"15927","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from Jumay' ibn Umayr, and he did not doubt, from his maternal uncle Abu Burda ibn Niyar, he said: I went with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Naqi' al-Musalla, and he put his hand into food then took it out, and it was adulterated or mixed. So he said: He who cheats us is not of us."
"15928","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, he said, Sulayman said to Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir: Narrate. So he narrated from Abu Burda ibn Niyar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No flogging above ten lashes except in a hadd from the hudud of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"15929","Abu Salama al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from Abu Burda ibn Niyar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No flogging above ten lashes except in a hadd from the hudud of Allah the Mighty and Majestic. And Layth had narrated it to us in Baghdad from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Bukayr, from Sulayman, then when we were in Egypt, Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj informed us."
"15930","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said, Sharik narrated to us, from Wa'il, from Jumay' ibn Umayr, from his maternal uncle, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the best earning. So he said: A blessed sale, and the work of a man with his hand."
"15931","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, al-Walid, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn Jumay', narrated to us, he said, Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm narrated to me, he said: I came with Zayd ibn Hasan, with Ibn Rummana the freed slave of Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan between us, we had set our hands for him and he was leaning on them inside the mosque, the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ibn Niyar, a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), forbade him, so he sent to Abu Bakr: Come to me. So he came to him and said: I saw Ibn Rummana between you leaning on you and on Zayd ibn Hasan. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The world shall not pass away until it is with Luka' son of Luka'."
